riddle_english:
It comes on shoulders, it goes on shoulders;
Though innocent, it gets beaten.
At worship and festivals, I am called upon;
Grand celebration is my life.

You play me with two hands;
To my rhythm, the heart begins to dance.
Grand celebration is my life.

Pieces move across the board;
The king stays in the middle.
The battle is fought with the strength of the mind;
No field is needed for it.

This game is a year-round pastime for children to pass the time while bathing; 
it’s played in the morning or evening, and Sundays are usually very crowded because 
many children gather at the river to bathe or just to play. What is this game?

Wherever they chant the uprising of the Egba people,
my name is never forgotten;
I am a thorn in the flesh of the Oyo Empire’s tax collectors.

There is a town with twelve houses; 
only two people live there, 
they feed each other and eat each other.

When I go, 
it follows me; 
when I stop, it stops; 
yet I cannot wrestle it to the ground or catch it.
